                            <comment id="14017691" author="fpj" created="Wed, 4 Jun 2014 13:33:15 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Patch looks good to me, but I couldn&apos;t reproduce the problem. I&apos;ve added an 127.0.1.1 entry to my /etc/hosts but I couldn&apos;t get the tests to fail without the patch. &lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14017704" author="ikelly" created="Wed, 4 Jun 2014 13:45:03 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;on a mac? It never happened me when I used a mac, seemed to automatically return the external ip. It did mean that moving networks while running tests caused failures though.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Also, the branch4.2 and trunk patches look very different, since trunk has BKTestConfiguration, which branch4.2 doesn&apos;t.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14017711" author="fpj" created="Wed, 4 Jun 2014 14:06:08 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;yes, I did try on a mac, let me try on ubuntu to see if I can reproduce it there.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="14017713" author="ikelly" created="Wed, 4 Jun 2014 14:09:41 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;happens to me on fedora 19 and debian wheezy.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
